            "file_text": "# Go vs JS Diff Function Comparison\n\n## Critical Findings So Far\n\n### MISSING PRIVATE FUNCTIONS IN GO:\nThese diff functions exist in JS but NOT found in Go:\n- `getConnectorDiff` (exists `getConnectorDiff`, wait need to verify)\n- `getConnectionDiff` (not found, only `getConnectionsDiff` for arrays)\n- `getModelDiff` (not found, only `getModelsDiff` for arrays)\n- `getPieceDiff` (not found, only `getPiecesDiff` for arrays)\n\nThe Go code has `getConnectors/Models/Connections/PiecesDiff` (plural - for arrays)\nBut appears to be missing the singular private functions.\n\n### CRITICAL LOGIC DIFFERENCES:\n\n**Connection Numeric Fields (Gap, Shift, Rise, etc):**\n- **JS**: Uses DELTAS - `diff.gap = after.gap - before.gap`\n- **JS Apply**: `result.gap = (base.gap ?? 0) + diff.gap` (adds delta)\n- **Go Apply**: `result.Gap = *diff.Gap` (replaces with value, not a delta!)\n\nThis is a MAJOR discrepancy that will cause test failures!\n\n## Functions to Compare in Detail:\n1. GetConnectorDiff - check if it exists and what it does\n2. GetConnectionDiff - check if it really doesn't exist \n3. GetPieceDiff - check if it really doesn't exist\n4. GetModelDiff - check if it really doesn't exist\n5. Point and Vector comparisons - look for delta vs absolute logic\n6. Tag, Concept, Port, File, Folder, Author diffs\n\n## Status:\nStill searching for these functions in their non-plural form...\n"
